{
  "id": "choose-a-visualization-read-a-stat", "title": "Read one number",
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "markdown", "content": "You'll distinguish a stat's latest value from an average over the selected period." },
    { "type": "section", "id": "read-stat", "title": "Inspect a stat's calculation", "blocks": [
      { "type": "interactive", "action": "navigate", "reftarget": "/d/Zb3f4veGk/stats?viewPanel=16&from=now-1h&to=now&timezone=browser", "verify": "on-page:/d/Zb3f4veGk", "content": "Open **Value only** on the **Stats** dashboard. Notice the single number and its unit." },
      { "type": "markdown", "content": "A stat makes one value prominent. It can show a current reading, but this example initially shows a mean. A large number alone doesn't tell you which calculation produced it." },
      { "type": "markdown", "content": "Open the panel menu and select **Edit**. Expand **Value options** if it's collapsed." },
      { "type": "interactive", "action": "highlight", "reftarget": "[id='reduceOptions.calcs']", "requirements": ["on-page:/d/Zb3f4veGk", "exists-reftarget"], "doIt": false, "content": "Find **Calculation** and notice **Mean**. Open the list and choose **Last** with the asterisk to display the latest non-null sample instead." },
      { "type": "markdown", "content": "Read the updated stat. **Mean** summarizes samples across the period; **Last** with the asterisk selects the most recent non-null sample returned by the query. Use the latter for a latest-reading question, and check the sample's freshness before calling it current." },
      { "type": "interactive", "action": "navigate", "reftarget": "/d/Zb3f4veGk/stats?viewPanel=16&from=now-1h&to=now&timezone=browser", "verify": "on-page:/d/Zb3f4veGk", "content": "Leave the editor without saving. The saved example still uses **Mean**." }
    ] },
    { "type": "markdown", "content": "You've read a stat and inspected the calculation behind its number. Choose it when the question needs one value rather than a trend or comparison." }
  ]
}